chatlogs/
/logs/*.*
/data/
data
/data/**
/evaluation/evaluation_set/*
/evaluation/function_set/*
/examples/output/*
/examples/metrics/*
/docs/writing/*
/docs/*.bkp
faasllm
*.txt
# ...except the Go harnesses, which are source despite the extension: they are
# //go:embed-ed (internal/builder/builder.go, evaluation/harness/harness.go),
# so a clone without them does not compile. They are .txt rather than .go
# because they reference handle(), which only exists once they are written next
# to a translated package.
!internal/builder/test_handler.txt
!evaluation/harness/bench_handler.go.txt
# ...and except the prediction study's human-readable result tables. The JSON
# beside them is machine-readable but not readable; these are the tables the
# write-up quotes, and for the same reason [I4] commits its CSV, a number in
# the thesis should be traceable to a file in the repo rather than to a run
# someone has to reproduce first.
!evaluation/prediction/*.txt
.env

.claude
# Evaluation run records. The directory is ignored by default, but the files
# that make a run reproducible and comparable across machines are tracked:
# the manifest (host, git commit, config sha256), the per-function outcome
# CSV, the append-only run log ([I1]'s feature->outcome training data), and
# the translated packages (so cmd/runtime can be re-measured on another host
# without paying for the translation again).
#
# Service logs stay ignored on purpose: they are large, and logs written
# before [F6] contain API keys in plaintext (see runs/service-20260807-*.log
# on the original dev machine). Never force-add one.
runs/*
!runs/manifest-*.txt
!runs/batch-*.csv
!runs/run-*.jsonl
!runs/packages-*.zip

# Python bytecode from evaluation/prediction's offline tooling
__pycache__/
*.pyc
